    "notes": "The mapped palace, garden waterways and theatre define the site frame. Local ground and water masks seat the stepped courts and uncover the authored basins. Surrounding terrain samples, roads and buildings remain in place. The original terrain, water and landcover return on unload. The footprint, channel locations and Water Stairway follow standard PMTiles. Flat court elevations, individual arches, seating and retaining walls are photo-based reconstructions fitted to standard viewer terrain. Water channels, fountain arcs and garden planting use static geometry and shared materials. Seasonal planting, temporary stage equipment and private interiors are outside the modeled exterior."
  },
